# Feedback UX (Zebra Android Tablet)

Prefer shared components from `src/components/feedback`. Never use system `Alert.alert` for these.

| Type | Component | Buttons | Blocks? | Use when |
|------|-----------|---------|---------|----------|
| Progress | `AppProgressModal` | None; Cancel only if abortable | Yes | Generate manifest, sync |
| Error | `AppErrorModal` | Retry and/or OK; optional Cancel / Support | Yes | Save/sync/print/photo failed |
| Success (milestone) | `AppSuccessModal` | OK | Yes | WO completed, must acknowledge |
| Success (routine) | `showToast()` | Auto-dismiss | No | Photo saved, label sent |
| Confirmation | `AppConfirmModal` | Cancel + Confirm (red if destructive) | Yes | Delete, void, reset |
| Warning | `AppWarningModal` | Cancel + Continue | Yes | Unusual weight, soft reminder |
| Recovery | `AppRecoveryModal` | Retry + Open Settings | Yes | No printer/scale/camera, jam |
| Field validation | Inline on control | — | No | Required fields in open form |
| Workflow lock | Dedicated overlay | Primary CTA only | Yes | Work paused, post-login sync |

## Progress nuance

- **Print label / documents:** non-blocking `showToast` (hardware side effect).
- **Generate manifest / heavy analysis:** blocking `AppProgressModal` (next step depends on result).

## Rules

- Never `Alert.alert('Success', …)` for capture/save/status.
- Never Alert for validation when a form/modal is already open.
- Demo all types: Settings → Debug (admin) → Feedback Modals Demo.
- Keep barcode container-delete and work-paused / sync locks as domain overlays.
